      "reasoning": "Now I have 2 untapped lands: Mystic Monastery and Plains. Armillary Sphere (2) is castable. That would let me fetch 2 basic lands, helping fix mana. Devil's Play isn't great to cast for X=0.\n\nI should cast Armillary Sphere to fix my mana. I have Mystic Monastery (WUR) and Plains (W). I can tap Mystic Monastery for {W}{U} or {W}{R} or {U}{R}. Probably tap for {W}{U} and use Plains for {W}, that's {W}{W}{U} which pays for Armillary Sphere's {2} cost.\n\nActually, wait - Armillary Sphere costs {2} (two generic). I need 2 generic mana. Mystic Monastery produces WUR - that's three colored mana. I could tap Mystic Monastery for WU, leaving R floating, but that's not efficient. Actually, I could tap Mystic Monastery for WU, and Plains for W, that's W+W+U = 3 mana. Armillary Sphere costs {2}, so I'd have 1 colored mana floating.\n\nI should probably tap Mystic Monastery for WU, Plains for W. That gives me W+W+U. Cast Armillary Sphere for {2} using 2 of those mana. The remaining mana (W or U) can't be used unless I have a spell with that color.\n\nActually, I have 2 untapped lands: Mystic Monastery and Plains. I should tap both to cast Armillary Sphere. Let me cast it and the system will ask for mana payment.\n\n\n\n",
