      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "THINK:\n1.  **Analyze the Error:** I received an `index_out_of_range` error. The message says \"Index 1 is out of range (no choices loaded). Call get_action_choices to see current options.\" This means that after I selected the Avenger trigger, the state changed, and the list of available triggered abilities is no longer what I thought it was.\n\n2.  **Hypothesize the Cause:** The game server likely processed my choice to stack the Avenger trigger. Now, it's presenting a new set of choices for the *next* trigger to stack. The indices have been updated. My previous plan to just call `index=1` is now invalid because the list of choices has changed.\n\n3.  **Corrective Action:** The error message explicitly tells me what to do: \"Call get_action_choices to see current options.\" This is the fundamental rule of the game loop. I must get the fresh state before I act.\n\n4.  **Execute the Correction:** I will call `get_action_choices()` to see the updated list of triggers I can stack. This will show me the new index for Aesi's ability.\n\n5.  **New Plan:**\n    *   Call `get_action_choices()`.\n    *   Identify the new index for \"Aesi, Tyrant of Gyre Strait\".\n    *   Call `choose_action()` with the correct, new index.Whoops, got a bit ahead of myself there, team. The game is telling me my playbook is out of date. It looks like when I put the Avenger's ability on the stack, the choices changed. My mistake.\n\nI need to get the latest information before making my next move. Let's call a quick timeout and look at the action choices again to make sure we get this right. One moment.",
