      "player": "DSV3 Stoic",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Wait, I need to check what happened. My life went from 40 to 28, so I took 12 damage. That must have been from Qwen3 Sarge's attackers. Let me check their board: they have a Hydra Broodmaster with 8/8 (summoning sickness removed now since I see it's turn 2), Plaxcaster Frogling (2/2 with counters), and Adrix and Nev (2/2). That's 12 power total.\n\nNow I'm at 28 life, opponent is at 40 life. I have 40 Pegasus tokens that are tapped (from attacking last turn), Pristine Angel is tapped, plus some lands and artifacts.\n\nI should probably play something defensive since my board is tapped. I have Ghostly Prison in hand - that could help prevent attacks. Or I could cast Mass Diminish to make all creatures 1/1s which would be effective against their 8/8 Hydra and 2/2 creatures.\n\nActually, let me think: my opponent has Adrix and Nev which doubles tokens. If they have token generation, that could be problematic. They also have Hydra Broodmaster which can make more hydras. Ghostly Prison would make it harder for them to attack.\n\nI should check Oracle text to be sure. Let me check Ghostly Prison and Mass Diminish.\n\n\n\n",
