      "reasoning": "Ghostly Prison is good against wide boards, especially if they're making tokens. Mass Diminish would make their Hydra 1/1, Plaxcaster 1/1, Adrix 1/1. That's powerful but only affects their current board, not future tokens.\n\nI should also consider Pristine Skywise which is a 6/4 Dragon with prowess and protection from instants. That's a good blocker and attacker.\n\nActually, I need to think about my strategy. I have a huge flying army that's currently tapped. I need to survive until next turn when I can untap and attack with 40 flyers plus Pristine Angel for lethal (44 damage).\n\nGhostly Prison would help survive. But actually, opponent only has 3 creatures currently (Hydra 8/8, Plaxcaster 2/2, Adrix 2/2). Paying 6 total to attack with all three might be manageable for them. Mass Diminish would reduce their threat significantly - their biggest threat becomes 1/1 instead of 8/8.\n\nI think Mass Diminish is better here. Cast it targeting Qwen3 Sarge. That makes all their creatures 1/1 until my next turn. Then next turn I can swing with my 40 flyers for lethal.\n\nActually wait, I should check if they have any mana to pay for Ghostly Prison. They have some lands and a Sol Ring. But Mass Diminish is just 1U, very cheap.\n\nLet me cast Mass Diminish targeting Qwen3 Sarge.\n\n",
