    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Bounced Prairie Stream (a dual land providing W/U) instead of a basic Plains when Boros Garrison already covers the white mana. Prairie Stream enters untapped with their basics, but a basic Plains is more redundant given Boros Garrison's {R}{W} production. They have Pristine Skywise and Mass Diminish in hand needing blue mana, making the U/W dual more valuable on board than an extra Plains.",
      "actionTaken": "Bounced Prairie Stream to hand with Boros Garrison's ETB trigger",
      "betterLine": "Bounce a basic Plains instead, since Boros Garrison already provides white mana and keeping Prairie Stream on board preserves blue mana access for Pristine Skywise and Mass Diminish",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 247,
      "player": "DSV3 Stoic",
      "decisionIndex": 242
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "GLM47 ESPN is at 6 life with no flying blockers. DSV3 Stoic has Pristine Angel (4/4 flying) and Devil's Play in hand. Attacking ESPN for 4 (to 2 life) then casting Devil's Play for X=2 (using Mountain + Sol Ring for {2}{R}) would eliminate a player this turn. Instead, they attacked Gem25P Coach at 24 life, dealing only chip damage.",
      "actionTaken": "Attacked Gem25P Coach (24 life) with Pristine Angel for 4 damage",
      "betterLine": "Attack GLM47 ESPN (6 life) with Pristine Angel for 4, then cast Devil's Play X=2 post-combat to eliminate ESPN entirely, removing a player from the game",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 249,
      "player": "DSV3 Stoic",
      "decisionIndex": 247
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Qwen3 Sarge passed the turn with 8 mana available (3 Islands, 2 Forests, Sol Ring) and multiple castable spells in hand, deploying nothing. Spawning Kraken (6 mana), Deekah (5 mana), Replication Technique (5 mana), and Nissa's Expedition (5 mana with convoke potential) were all castable. With GLM47 ESPN at 1 life and needing board presence, wasting an entire turn's worth of mana is a significant tempo loss.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed the turn without casting any spells despite having 8 available mana and multiple castable options.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Spawning Kraken (6 mana) to establish a major threat, or Deekah, Fractal Theorist (5 mana) to start generating token value from future spells, or Nissa's Expedition to ramp toward Ezuri's Predation.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 260,
      "player": "Qwen3 Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 263
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem25P Coach is sending Avenger of Zendikar (5/5) at GLM47 ESPN who is at 1 life, when a single Plant token could deal lethal. This wastes the Avenger's 5 power that could have been directed at Qwen3 Sarge (40 life) or DSV3 Stoic (40 life). Since Qwen3 Sarge's creatures are tapped, sending Aesi + Avenger at Sarge would deal 10 unblocked damage.",
      "actionTaken": "Selected Avenger of Zendikar to attack GLM47 ESPN (1 life), overkilling by 4+ damage",
      "betterLine": "Send a single Plant token at GLM47 ESPN for lethal, and direct Avenger of Zendikar and Aesi at Qwen3 Sarge (or DSV3 Stoic) to apply meaningful pressure to the remaining opponents",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 269,
      "player": "Gem25P Coach",
      "decisionIndex": 270
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "DSV3 Stoic casts Storm Herd for 10 mana (8WW) to create 40 1/1 Pegasus tokens with flying while at 40 life. However, Qwen3 Sarge has Adrix and Nev, Twincasters on the board which could double token creation if they copy Storm Herd somehow, and more importantly, the opponent Qwen3 Sarge still has resources. The main concern is that DSV3 Stoic should consider whether to play a land first (they have Island, Mountain, Plains, Prairie Stream in hand) before casting Storm Herd. With 8 lands on board, they need all 8 to cast Storm Herd (8WW requires exactly Sol Ring + Izzet Locket + lands). Looking at the mana: Sol Ring (2 colorless), Izzet Locket (1 U or R), Mystic Monastery (U/R/W), Plains (W), Mountain (R), Plains (W), Island (U), Pristine Angel is a creature not a land. That's 7 lands + Sol Ring + Izzet Locket = 9 mana sources producing at most 10 mana. They need 8WW - they can get WW from two Plains, and the rest from other sources. This works. But they didn't play a land first. Playing a land before casting Storm Herd costs nothing and would give them more mana available for future turns. This is a minor sequencing error - they should play a land (like Prairie Stream or Island) before casting Storm Herd.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Storm Herd without first playing a land drop for the turn.",
      "betterLine": "Play a land (e.g., Prairie Stream or Island) first, then cast Storm Herd. The land drop is free and would provide additional mana on future turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 275,
      "player": "DSV3 Stoic",
      "decisionIndex": 305
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Plant tokens cannot block Pristine Angel because it has flying and plants lack flying/reach. The player attempted an illegal block instead of using Simic Charm to bounce the attacking Pristine Angel, which would have saved 4 damage at 18 life.",
      "actionTaken": "Attempted to block flying Pristine Angel with a ground-only Plant token, which is an illegal block",
      "betterLine": "Cast Simic Charm choosing the bounce mode to return Pristine Angel to DSV3 Stoic's hand, preventing 4 damage and temporarily removing the threat",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 279,
      "player": "Gem25P Coach",
      "decisionIndex": 310
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With 8 mana available (4 forests, 3 islands, Sol Ring), Qwen3 Sarge chose Hydra Broodmaster (4GG = 6 mana) over potentially more impactful plays. Nissa's Expedition with convoke could ramp significantly by tapping Adrix and Nev and Plaxcaster Frogling to help cast it, fetching 2 lands and setting up for Ezuri's Predation next turn. Replication Technique (4U = 5 mana) copying Adrix and Nev (doubling token production even further) or Plaxcaster Frogling could also be strong. However, Hydra Broodmaster is a 7/7 that threatens a massive token army later with its monstrosity ability, especially with Adrix and Nev doubling the tokens. The main concern is that casting Hydra Broodmaster leaves only 2 mana open and doesn't immediately impact the board, while Replication Technique on Adrix and Nev would set up exponential token doubling. With only two opponents remaining (GLM47 ESPN is at -9hp, eliminated), and Gem25P Coach at 14hp with Aesi on board, the Hydra Broodmaster's monstrosity activation won't come online for a while. Replication Technique copying Adrix and Nev would quadruple future tokens and could be game-winning with Ezuri's Predation.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Hydra Broodmaster (6 mana), leaving 2 mana unused with no immediate board impact beyond a vanilla 7/7.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Replication Technique (5 mana) targeting Adrix and Nev, Twincasters to create a copy (quadrupling future token creation), then use remaining 3 mana for other plays. This sets up a devastating Ezuri's Predation on a future turn with quadrupled tokens.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 284,
      "player": "Qwen3 Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 318
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to graft a +1/+1 counter onto Hydra Broodmaster. This is a missed opportunity because having a +1/+1 counter on Hydra Broodmaster enables Plaxcaster Frogling's activated ability to grant it shroud, protecting a key threat that can generate massive tokens via Monstrosity. The +1/+1 stat boost is marginal, but the shroud protection is meaningful.",
      "actionTaken": "Declined the Graft trigger, leaving Hydra Broodmaster without a +1/+1 counter.",
      "betterLine": "Accept the Graft trigger to place a +1/+1 counter on Hydra Broodmaster, enabling Plaxcaster Frogling to grant it shroud protection for {2}.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 287,
      "player": "Qwen3 Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 321
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "DSV3 Stoic has Pristine Angel (4/4 flying) on board and Pristine Skywise (6/4 flying) in hand. Gem25P Coach is at exactly 10 life with no flying blockers (Aesi is a 5/5 ground creature). Casting Pristine Skywise and attacking with both flyers would deal exactly 10 damage for lethal. DSV3 Stoic has the mana: Plains+Plains+Island+Mystic Monastery+Sol Ring+Izzet Locket covers the 4WU cost. Instead, they passed without doing anything in precombat main.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed the precombat main phase without casting any spells or playing a land.",
      "betterLine": "Play Mountain, cast Pristine Skywise (4WU) using available mana, then go to combat and attack Gem25P Coach with both Pristine Angel (4/4) and Pristine Skywise (6/4) for exactly 10 flying damage = lethal.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 297,
      "player": "DSV3 Stoic",
      "decisionIndex": 332
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "DSV3 Stoic passed the turn without playing a land (has Mountain and Plains in hand) and without casting Pristine Skywise (6/4 flyer for 4WU, which is castable with available mana). In a 1v1 against a 40-life opponent, deploying a 6/4 flying threat and making a land drop are both important to establish a clock.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority without playing any spells or lands in postcombat main phase.",
      "betterLine": "Play Mountain (or Plains) as a land drop, then cast Pristine Skywise (4WU) using available mana to establish a flying threat alongside Pristine Angel.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 302,
      "player": "DSV3 Stoic",
      "decisionIndex": 341
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "DSV3 Stoic cast Pristine Skywise before playing a land from hand. They have Mountain and Plains in hand and appear to have not yet made their land drop this turn. Playing a land first is free and would give them an additional mana source, which could matter for future plays or if they draw into something useful.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Pristine Skywise without first playing a land from hand",
      "betterLine": "Play Plains (or Mountain) first, then cast Pristine Skywise with the additional mana available",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 311,
      "player": "DSV3 Stoic",
      "decisionIndex": 356
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "DSV3 Stoic cast Ghostly Prison before playing a land. They had Mountain and Plains in hand and hadn't used their land drop yet. Playing a land first (likely Mountain for future Devil's Play/Increasing Vengeance flexibility) before casting spells is standard correct sequencing, as it maximizes available mana and preserves options.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Ghostly Prison without first making a land drop",
      "betterLine": "Play Mountain (or Plains) first, then cast Ghostly Prison",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 313,
      "player": "DSV3 Stoic",
      "decisionIndex": 361
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "If Hydra Broodmaster is on the battlefield (implied by being in the choices), declining to activate its Monstrosity ability with Adrix and Nev (token doubler) on the field is a missed opportunity to build a massive board. With available mana, they could create multiple large Hydra tokens doubled by Adrix and Nev, putting enormous pressure on DSV3 Stoic who only has Pristine Angel as a threat.",
      "actionTaken": "Declined to activate any abilities during postcombat main phase",
      "betterLine": "Activate Hydra Broodmaster's Monstrosity ability for X=2 or X=3 (depending on available mana), creating doubled tokens via Adrix and Nev to overwhelm the opponent",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 315,
      "player": "Qwen3 Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 363
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Qwen3 Sarge skipped attacking the sole remaining opponent (DSV3 Stoic at 28 life) when DSV3 Stoic was completely tapped out. Pristine Angel can only block one attacker, meaning at least two creatures would deal unblocked damage. With Hydra Broodmaster (7/7), Adrix and Nev (2/2), and Plaxcaster Frogling, attacking would push through significant damage (likely 9+ points) with no risk since Stoic has no mana available for tricks.",
      "actionTaken": "Skipped the attack phase entirely, dealing 0 damage.",
      "betterLine": "Attack with all creatures. Pristine Angel (protection from colors while untapped) can block one colored creature without taking damage, but the remaining attackers get through for significant damage. Even in the worst case, this is free damage against a tapped-out opponent in a 1v1 situation.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 317,
      "player": "Qwen3 Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 363
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to activate Hydra Broodmaster's Monstrosity ability in a 1v1 situation against an opponent at 28hp. With available mana (3 Forests + 3 Islands + Sol Ring = ~7 mana), they could activate Monstrosity for X=3, creating 3 3/3 Hydra tokens doubled to 6 by Adrix and Nev (18 total power). This would create significant board pressure against DSV3 Stoic who only has Pristine Angel as a creature.",
      "actionTaken": "Declined all activated abilities including Hydra Broodmaster's Monstrosity",
      "betterLine": "Activate Hydra Broodmaster's Monstrosity for X=3, creating 6 3/3 Hydra tokens (doubled by Adrix and Nev) to build overwhelming board presence for the following turn",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 320,
      "player": "Qwen3 Sarge",
      "decisionIndex": 368
    }
  ],
